{
  "title": "Investigate Design Node Click Freeze",
  "status": "closed",
  "prompt": "Investigate why clicking a React Flow node in Design.tsx causes browser page freeze",
  "summary": "Investigated Design.tsx node click freeze. Root cause: selection state is baked into baseNodes useMemo (line 5937), causing all 180 nodes to be recreated on every selection change, which triggers React Flow onSelectionChange again in a feedback loop. Contributing factors: XState handler always creates new state reference (no semantic equality), panel sections torn down/rebuilt on selection change (line 8090), and guardedSetter identity instability. The arePortsCompatible change at line 6935 is NOT related (only fires during drag). Recommended fixes documented in ticket.",
